         /home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting/wrong_p
         ort_5000                                                               
         fi                                                                     
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         4. Delete the existing Pod (if present) and re-create it from the      
         corrected manifest                                                     
         ```bash                                                                
         kubectl delete pod kube-wrong-port-5000 --ignore-not-found             
         kubectl apply -f                                                       
         /home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting/wrong_p
         ort_5000/wrong_port_5000.yaml                                          
         kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready pod/kube-wrong-port-5000            
         --timeout=60s                                                          
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         5. Verify the application responds to HTTP on port 5000 from inside the
         container (one-shot check)                                             
         ```bash                                                                
         kubectl exec pod/kube-wrong-port-5000 -- python3 -c "import            
         urllib.request;                                                        
         print(urllib.request.urlopen('http://127.0.0.1:5000/').getcode())"     
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         6. Optional cluster-network verification and quick log check (if step 5
         still fails)                                                           
         ```bash                                                                
         POD_IP=$(kubectl get pod kube-wrong-port-5000 -o                       
         jsonpath='{.status.podIP}')                                            
         echo "Pod IP: $POD_IP"                                                 
         curl -sS --max-time 5 "http://$POD_IP:5000/" || echo "HTTP to pod IP   
         failed"                                                                
         kubectl logs pod/kube-wrong-port-5000 --tail=200                       
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         Notes:                                                                 
         - The root cause is a mismatch: the Python server listens on 5000 while
         manifest/Dockerfile advertised port 80. Steps above make the declared  
         configuration match the running app and rebuild the image so the       
         cluster uses the corrected image.                                      
         - If your cluster is not minikube and does not share your local Docker 
         daemon, you will need to make the rebuilt image available to the       
         cluster (registry or other image loading mechanism). If that is the    
